perimental Design:** One-shot LLM evaluation without fine-tuning, ablations, or error analysis provides limited insight into model capabilities or benchmark utility. The case studies in Appendix A.6 are illustrative but not systematic.\n\n6. **Practical Applicability:** Despite claiming real-world utility, we provide no validation of sim-to-real transfer. Section 7 correctly characterizes this as future work, which undermines claims of practical value.\n\n**On the Proposed Revisions:**\n\nThe reviewer has correctly noted that our rebuttal proposes improvements not present in the submission. This is a fundamental point: evaluation must be based on the paper as written, not on promised future work. The proposed additions (embodied AI baselines, human evaluation, task-specific metrics, error analysis, sim-to-real validation) would require substantial new experiments. While we believe these are necessary for a strong paper, they are not part of the current submission.\n\n**Appropriate Venue and Path Forward:**\n\nWe agree with the reviewer's assessment that the paper is best characterized as 'a useful engineering contribution (platform + dataset)' rather than a methodological advance suitable for a top-tier ML venue. The work has value for the community as a released resource and dataset, but does not meet the standards for acceptance at a selective machine learning conference. The paper would be better suited for:\n- A workshop or applications track at a major conference\n- A datasets and benchmarks venue (e.g., NeurIPS Datasets and Benchmarks track, ICLR Benchmarks)\n- A robotics or embodied AI-specific venue\n\n**Commitment to Strengthening the Work:**\n\nIf we revise for resubmission, we commit to addressing the core limitations:\n\n1. Include comparisons with embodied AI baselines (at least 2-3 specialized vision-language models and RL agents)\n2. Add human evaluation studies with inter-annotator agreement metrics\n3. Introduce task-specific evaluation metrics beyond standard NLG metrics\n4. Provide systematic error analysis and ablation studies\n5. Conduct preliminary sim-to-real validation (even if limited in scope)\n6. Revise framing to accurately reflect contribution as comprehensive system integration rather than methodological novelty\n7. Document and release inter-annotator agreement statistics and annotation guidelines\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\nYour rebuttal evaluation is fair and accurate. The submission presents solid engineering and a potentially useful resource for the community, but lacks the novel methodology, comprehensive empirical validation, and demonstrated practical impact necessary for a top-tier ML conference. We maintain the REJECT decision as appropriate and will use this feedback to strengthen the work for a more suitable venue."
