claims of superiority can be supported.\n\n**Statistical Validation:**\nAll reported improvements (5.6%, 7.7% in Tables 5-6) lack confidence intervals or significance tests. With small test sets (~60 samples at 20% of 297-300 total), these differences may be within noise. We did not conduct the rigorous statistical analysis required.\n\n**Presentation Issues:**\nWe acknowledge numerous writing errors ('it;s kind', 'accosication', 'aditionally', 'imabalce') and non-standard equation numbering ('(ℑ)', '(Σ)', '(T)') that appear to be formatting errors. These should be corrected to standard numbering (3), (4), (5), etc. The form-invariance explanation (Section 3.1.1) is convoluted and should be clarified.\n\n**Qualitative Spectrographic Analysis:**\nSection 5.1 relies on subjective descriptions of cherry-picked spectrograms without quantitative group-level statistics. Proper analysis would require metrics like pitch perturbation, spectral stability indices, and statistical group comparisons (ANOVA).\n\n**Missing Ablation and Baseline Comparisons:**\nWe did not isolate which CQCC components (CQT magnitude, resampling, DCT) drive improvements, nor did we compare against modern deep learning baselines or contemporary features like Mel-spectrograms. These are standard comparisons in 2024.\n\n**Path Forward:**\nIf we revise this work, the essential changes would include:\n1. Stratified k-fold cross-validation with proper statistical testing\n2. Investigation and resolution of SVM underperformance\n3. Comprehensive ablation studies\n4. Comparison with deep learning and modern baselines\n5. Quantitative spectrographic analysis\n6. Extensive proofreading and presentation fixes\n7. Repositioning the contribution as an application study with proper caveats about generalization\n\nWe recognize these revisions are substantial and require new experiments. The current submission does not meet the standards for acceptance at a selective venue due to unsound experimental methodology, inconsistent results, and presentation issues. We thank the reviewer for identifying these critical flaws."
