d on Figure 8 convergence).\n\n- **Failure modes:** Beyond BookCorpus, our framework succeeds on all tested vision and Tiny Shakespeare tasks. This suggests the approach is reasonably robust within its tested scope. We do not have evidence of failure modes other than the BookCorpus language task, which we discuss transparently.\n\n**Conclusion**\n\nWe view your review as identifying important directions for future work: scaling to larger models, deeper investigation of language model alignment, and practical cost quantification. These do not invalidate our core contributions—a unified symmetry framework and the first demonstration of zero-barrier LMC for Transformers on multiple domains—but they appropriately calibrate the scope of the current work. We believe the paper makes sufficient contributions for acceptance, with honest acknowledgment of limitations, and we fully expect follow-up work to address scaling and extend the approach to larger, contemporary models."
